            <ArticleTitle>[THE COGNITIVE STATUS OF PATIENTS WITH TYPE 2 DIABETES MELLITUS AFTER CORONARY BYPASS SURGERY].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>39-44</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of the study was to evaluate the neuropsychological status of patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus (DM2) before and I year after coronary bypass surgery performed under conditions of artificial circulation. It included 114 patients (54 with and 60 without DM2). Prior to surgery, the patients with DM2 had positive characteristics of neurodynamics and attention. They deteriorated 1 year after coronary bypass surgery, but improved in the patients without DM2.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
